sec.p:
A review of the literature yielded few a priori criteria for defining mitigation success beyond the 5pp tolerance of subgroup disparity established by Gianatassio et al. 22. We derived success criteria to align with clinically meaningful thresholds within our system. As our objective was to minimize disparities between subgroups, not just to improve subgroup fairness metrics, we report criteria using both absolute EOD and non-absolute EOD. In this study, mitigation was considered successful if:
Alert rate changed ≤20% relative to baseline and accuracy dropped no more than 10% relative to baseline;
Absolute EOD <5pp for all subgroups of target class;
Bias did not meaningfully increase among non-target classes, as defined below.
